@@ -327,6 +328,12 @@ To properly configure your reverse proxy (securely), please consult it's documen
 To enable the builtin openAPI interface (Swagger UI), specify `"enable_openapi": true` in the api_server configuration.
 This will enable the Swagger UI at the `/docs` endpoint. By default, that's running at <http://localhost:8080/docs> - but it'll depend on your settings.
 
+### Response compression
+
+By default, API responses larger than 1KB are compressed using gzip.
+Both the UI and API clients will transparently decompress these responses, which can considerably reduce the transfer size for data-heavy endpoints (e.g. trade history, which can easily be multiple megabytes).
+This can be disabled by setting `"enable_gzip": false` in the api_server configuration.
+
 ### Advanced API usage using JWT tokens
 
